  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WASH Systems for Health (WS4H)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The WASH System for Health (WS4H) is a 4-year programme (2024-2028) developed by the UK&apos;s FCDO to strengthen the systems needed to establish reliable, resilient, and inclusive WASH. It is related to the &apos;Proposal for Strengthening WASH Systems for Health in Nigeria and Sierra Leone&apos;. It aims to Strengthening WASH Systems to ensure sustainable WASH service delivery, including planning, budgeting and accountability processes, testing service delivery models, and attract new public and private finance to accelerate progress towards SDG 6 WASH.WS4H is funded by FCDO and SHA leads the consortium for West Africa with GOAL being the main partner in Sierra Leone. In Nigeria, the programme is located in Kano and Cross River States, with a learning component in North West Nigeria.First point of contact at FCDO: Almaz Akainyah</narrative>
  </description>
